{"id": "EUVD-2026-59387", "enisaUuid": "d338f695-eac9-3fe9-b796-50319f2a782a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsoundwire: fix bug in sdw_add_element_group_count found by syzkaller\n\nThe original implementation caused an out-of-bounds memory access\nin the sdw_add_element_group_count for-loop when i == num.\n\nfor (i = 0; i <= num; i++) {\n    if (rate == group->rates[i] && lane == group->lanes[i])\n        ...\n\nTo fix this error, the function now checks for existing rate/lane\nentries in the group(a function parameter) using a for-loop before\nadding them.\n\nNo functional changes apart from this fix.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:57:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:45:00", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a2275dce05e6d1cce69bf68f23ea7a63c0c54bae", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5c3ce6d3559ce57e6c3108aa9ecf7b32764188c5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a454f61747c97e2eadaa7a35ffc1f4b1645c6a53", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e483a406a23a92d5202e8d324f206e127eef48ff", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f772ff5a0e6758fd412803c09e03ba3bca5f5878"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-72488", "GHSA-m46v-696m-pmpf"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0fbf8f8b-db00-3483-a622-5c56a4f16c5e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9026118f20e28f202dab34f219bbb831ffb8c4dc <a454f61747c97e2eadaa7a35ffc1f4b1645c6a53"}, {"id": "1a8ad12a-0900-313f-b7df-177cfb53155e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9026118f20e28f202dab34f219bbb831ffb8c4dc <5c3ce6d3559ce57e6c3108aa9ecf7b32764188c5"}, {"id": "1a8dabd5-2f5b-315b-96e9-2f73261ee4da", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.10"}, {"id": "5b8aca43-d2a2-3ce8-936b-6260b15adb39", "product": {"name": "Linux", "ve